<!--
    arm64e virtual calls resolved by pointer-auth discriminator
    (`option arm64evcall on|off`).

    Issue: an arm64e C++ virtual call loads its target from a vtable slot and
    authenticates it with `blraa`/`braa`, so it renders as
    `(**(code **)(*obj + off))(...)` with no hint of the method. iOS 16.4.1
    debugserver has 295 such sites.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement. `analyzers/rtti/kuna_arm64evcall.rs`
    indexes every run of IA-signed, address-diversified `__const` slots by
    (index in run, diversifier) from the chained fixups, walks back from each
    call to its `movk #d, lsl #48` and the authenticated vtable-pointer load,
    and the flow builds the CALLIND as a direct call when the slot holds one
    method, or warns with the candidates when it holds several.

    P0 assertion: `option arm64evcall on|off`.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture; every pass loads
    a fixture through the object bootstrap (see the fixtures READMEs):
    `macho_arm64e_vcall` (two vtables `{A_f, A_g}` and `{B_f, A_g}`),
    `macho_arm64e_vcall_shapes` (a slot 32 words in, reached by adding a
    constant register, and a Swift class metadata located by its signed
    `Description`), and the kernel collection `kernelcache/fileset_vcall.macho`
    (a kernel vtable `{Base_m0, Base_m1}` and a kext vtable
    `{Base_m0, Widget_m1}`), loaded at its kernel entry.

    Passes 1, 3 and 5 (`option arm64evcall off`) reproduce the BUG: every call
    is an anonymous slot call.
    Passes 2, 4 and 6 (`option arm64evcall on`, the shipped default) are the
    FIX: `_call_g` calls `_A_g` (slot 1 holds it in both vtables) and `_call_f`
    names its two candidates; `_call_big` calls `_C_m`, `_call_swift`
    `_S_m2` and `_call_swift_m3` `_S_m3` with no argument (the method pointer
    left in `x8` is not a hidden-return buffer); the kernel's slot-0 call is `Base_m0`, and its slot-1 call names
    the kext's override, which only the whole collection's slots show (the
    entry's own image keeps no signing context once the collection's fixups
    are applied).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
